  "scientific_takeaway": "Under 5-fold event-grouped cross-validation across 11 independent flood events (39 positive days), Logistic Regression (Balanced) achieved the highest out-of-fold ROC-AUC of 0.9222 and PR-AUC of 0.1750 with an event capture recall of 71.79% (28/39 positive days captured), accompanied by a false alarm rate of 10.46% (187 false positives). Random Forest (Balanced) achieved ROC-AUC of 0.9023, PR-AUC of 0.1008, and recall of 41.03% (16/39 captured). XGBoost (Calibrated Scale) achieved ROC-AUC of 0.8693 with conservative predictions (recall 7.69%, 3/39 captured, 1.96% false alarm rate). Given the small sample size of 11 independent flood episodes across 2020-2024 (2 to 3 events per test fold), variance is substantial and all models must strictly retain their status as EXPERIMENTAL_EXPLORATORY_BASELINE rather than autonomous operational triggers."
